§ `s 122(1), (3) -- must I give evidence`

#ASSERT `Can I be made to give evidence` `criminal proceedings against me` EQUALS `I am competent to give evidence but cannot be compelled to`
#ASSERT `Can I be made to give evidence` `civil proceedings to which I am a party` EQUALS `I am a competent witness, and whether I can be compelled is not covered by this encoding`

§ `s 122(4) to (8), 56(4) -- questions about my past and my character`

#ASSERT `Must I answer a question about my past or my character` `I stay silent and do not give evidence` EQUALS `I am not cross-examined, because I have not given evidence`
#ASSERT `Must I answer a question about my past or my character` `asked about a previous conviction, nothing more` EQUALS `it must not be asked, and if asked I need not answer it`
#ASSERT `Must I answer a question about my past or my character` `asked about my alibi witness's name` EQUALS `section 122(4) does not reach this question`
#ASSERT `Must I answer a question about my past or my character` `asked about a similar offence admissible to prove the offence charged` EQUALS `it may be asked`
#ASSERT `Must I answer a question about my past or my character` `asked about my bad reputation, admissible to clear my co-accused` EQUALS `it may be asked`
#ASSERT `Must I answer a question about my past or my character` `asked about a conviction after I testified against my co-accused` EQUALS `it may be asked`
#ASSERT `Must I answer a question about my past or my character` `asked about my bad reputation after I called a character witness` EQUALS `it may be asked`
#ASSERT `Must I answer a question about my past or my character` `I attacked the prosecution witness's record; the question goes to my credibility` EQUALS `it may be asked`
#ASSERT `Must I answer a question about my past or my character` `I attacked the prosecution witness's record; the question does not go to my credibility` EQUALS `the court is not to permit it`

§ `s 134(4), (6) -- refusing to answer because it would incriminate me`

#ASSERT `May I refuse to answer because it would incriminate me` `the answer would tend to prove the offence charged` EQUALS `I am not entitled to refuse`
#ASSERT `May I refuse to answer because it would incriminate me` `the answer would expose me to another prosecution` EQUALS `I am not entitled to refuse`
#ASSERT `May I refuse to answer because it would incriminate me` `the answer would expose my wife to a prosecution` EQUALS `I am not entitled to refuse`
#ASSERT `May I refuse to answer because it would incriminate me` `another prosecution, on a question going only to my credibility` EQUALS `section 134(4) does not take away a right to refuse, and whether I have one is not covered by this encoding`
#ASSERT `May I refuse to answer because it would incriminate me` `another prosecution, on a credibility question asked under section 56` EQUALS `I am not entitled to refuse`
#ASSERT `May I refuse to answer because it would incriminate me` `the offence charged, on a question going only to my credibility` EQUALS `I am not entitled to refuse`

#ASSERT `Can my compelled answer be proved against me in proceedings for another offence` `the answer would tend to prove the offence charged` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can my compelled answer be proved against me in proceedings for another offence` `the answer would expose me to another prosecution` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my compelled answer be proved against me in proceedings for another offence` `another prosecution, on a question going only to my credibility` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `ss 103, 105 to 108 -- which facts I must prove`

#ASSERT `Must I prove this fact` `that I committed the offence charged` EQUALS `the burden is on the prosecution`
#ASSERT `Must I prove this fact` `that I admitted the offence to someone` EQUALS `the burden is on the prosecution`
#ASSERT `Must I prove this fact` `circumstances bringing my case within a general exception in the Penal Code` EQUALS `the burden is on me, and the court is to presume those circumstances absent`
#ASSERT `Must I prove this fact` `circumstances bringing my case within a special exception or proviso in the Penal Code or the law defining the offence` EQUALS `the burden is on me, and the court is to presume those circumstances absent`
#ASSERT `Must I prove this fact` `that I was elsewhere at the time` EQUALS `the burden is on me`
#ASSERT `Must I prove this fact` `a fact especially within my knowledge` EQUALS `the burden is on me`
#ASSERT `Must I prove this fact` `a fact that must be proved before evidence I wish to give is admissible` EQUALS `the burden is on me`

§ `ss 17, 21 -- my statements, admissions and confessions`

#ASSERT `Is my statement a confession` `I told the officer I took the money`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my statement a confession` `I said I was near the shop that night`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my statement a confession` `I said something with no bearing on any fact in issue`

#ASSERT NOT `Is my statement an admission` `I said something with no bearing on any fact in issue`

#ASSERT NOT `Can I prove my own admission in my favour` `I told the officer I took the money`
#ASSERT `Can I prove my own admission in my favour` `a letter I dated at Penang on the day of the crime`

§ `ss 54 to 56 -- my character`

#ASSERT `Is my character relevant to whether I did what I am accused of` `my criminal trial, I say nothing of my character`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my character relevant to whether I did what I am accused of` `a civil suit, my character not otherwise relevant`
#ASSERT `Is my character relevant to whether I did what I am accused of` `a civil suit, my character appears from facts otherwise relevant`

#ASSERT `Can my bad character be proved against me under section 56` `my criminal trial, I say nothing of my character` EQUALS `not under section 56, which I have not opened`
#ASSERT `Can my bad character be proved against me under section 56` `my criminal trial, I cross-examine to show my good reputation` EQUALS `yes, evidence of my bad disposition or reputation, and of my previous convictions`
#ASSERT `Can my bad character be proved against me under section 56` `a civil suit, my character not otherwise relevant` EQUALS `section 56 applies only in criminal proceedings`

§ `s 124 -- what I told my wife or husband`

#ASSERT `Is the offence charged a specified offence` `a child abuse offence against a 15-year-old`
#ASSERT NOT `Is the offence charged a specified offence` `a child abuse offence against my adult domestic worker`
#ASSERT `Is the offence charged a specified offence` `a sexual offence against my domestic worker`
#ASSERT `Is the offence charged a specified offence` `a Chapter 16 offence against a vulnerable person in my care`
#ASSERT NOT `Is the offence charged a specified offence` `a cheating offence against a 10-year-old`

#ASSERT `Can my wife or husband be made to disclose what I told them` `what I told my wife, at my trial for a sexual offence against an adult` EQUALS `no, my wife or husband cannot be compelled to disclose it`
#ASSERT `Can my wife or husband be made to disclose what I told them` `what I told my wife, at my trial for child abuse of a 15-year-old` EQUALS `section 124 does not protect it`
#ASSERT `Can my wife or husband be made to disclose what I told them` `what I told her before we married` EQUALS `section 124 does not protect it`
#ASSERT `Can my wife or husband be made to disclose what I told them` `what I told my wife, at my trial for hurting her` EQUALS `not covered by this encoding, because section 124(1) does not say whether its exception reaches the compulsion limb`

#ASSERT NOT `May my wife or husband disclose what I told them` `what I told my wife, at my trial for a sexual offence against an adult`
#ASSERT `May my wife or husband disclose what I told them` `what I told my wife, at my trial for hurting her`

§ `ss 128, 130, 131 -- what passed between me and my lawyer`

#ASSERT NOT `May my lawyer disclose it` `I told my solicitor I committed forgery and asked to be defended`
#ASSERT `May my lawyer disclose it` `I asked my solicitor to sue on a forged deed`
#ASSERT `May my lawyer disclose it` `my solicitor saw a new entry made in my account book during the case`
#ASSERT NOT `May my lawyer disclose it` `my solicitor's advice, after I gave evidence myself`
#ASSERT `May my lawyer disclose it` `my communication, after I called my solicitor and asked about it`

#ASSERT NOT `Can I be made to disclose a confidential communication with my lawyer` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be made to disclose a confidential communication with my lawyer` TRUE TRUE

§ `ss 135, 136 -- how many witnesses`

#ASSERT NOT `Does the Act require more witnesses or corroboration before a fact is proved against me` 1 TRUE

